From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The party in the lower menu's panel (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the 3DS remaster's lower menu, the party shows in the panel, laid out
tall as its approved mock-up has it, and comes and goes as the bag does;
the summary shows there too, and the panel's apps hand over to each other
behind its black:

- Opened while the platform can show the menu
  (NitroPort_LowerMenuAvailable), the party puts its main screen (the
  panels, the message, CANCEL) on the lower screen (the DS's screen swap),
  248 lines tall; the upper screen keeps the field; the touch screen (the
  Poké Balls) isn't shown, so the panel's touches are nobody's.
- Each row of panels 16 pixels lower than the one above it (the first 16,
  the second 32, the third 48): the panels' templates, their windows,
  their sprites, the cursor's places (PARTY_PORT_TALL_SLOT_DY); what was
  under them 56 lower, at the bottom: the message's windows, CANCEL and
  CONFIRM, a Pokémon's menu, YES/NO (PARTY_PORT_TALL_BOTTOM_DY).
- The background (BG3) drawn anew when the party opens, from its own
  tiles, by the rules the mock-up was made with: the stripes from 7, 7, the
  panels' rows of the DS's background each moved with its row, the teal
  bands between the columns run on along the DS's diagonal from one panel
  to the next, the dashed line beside each right panel, the message's rows
  56 lower (PartyPortTall_LayOutBackground: its tiles after the party's
  own). The second left panel without its top edge (PartyPortTall_FixEdges,
  as panels are drawn and switched; an empty one too). A form change's 3D
  sparkles at the icon moved with its row.
- From the lower menu, POKéMON fades the panel to black, the party comes
  behind it and pops in; B, CANCEL or POKéMON again fade it to black, and
  the map fades in once the field's back. While the cursor waits on the
  panels, the menu's other buttons work: BAG switches to the bag in the
  panel (POKéMON in the bag back to the party: StartMenu_PortSwitchFromApp,
  the bag's StartMenu_PortSwitchFromBag made the two apps'), TRAINER,
  POKéDEX and OPTIONS open straight from it, SAVE, MAP and POKéTCH are acted
  on in the field. A tap on the menu while the party's busy, before it's
  shown, or in a party not the menu's: nobody's (the bag's the same, so a
  quick second tap on BAG doesn't close the bag it opened).
- The summary in the panel: from the party in the panel, its main screen
  (the pages, the Pokémon) on the lower screen at the DS's size, none of
  the wider upper screen's layouts; its touch screen not shown; the upper
  screen keeping the field.
- The panel's apps hand over behind its black: an app leaving for another
  of them (the party for the summary, the bag to give an item, back to the
  bag; the bag for the party, an item used on a Pokémon or given; the
  summary back to the party) fades the panel to black, the menu kept on
  (NitroPort_LowerMenuKeepShown), and the next one finds it so
  (NitroPort_LowerMenuKeptShown) and pops in (PartyPort_LeavesInPanel,
  BagPort_LeavesInPanel: the bag's fades out put off to its last state,
  which decides). The start menu opens them (StartMenu_PortAppIsMenus: the
  field's own app, its task the field's; not an app's own, the Poffin
  Case's party) and, each gone, knows how (StartMenu_PortAppGone); the
  menu still kept when the player walks again, it's let go. Left another
  way (a field move, the mail, an evolution), the DS's fades.
- With the classic display (no menu), the party, the bag and the summary
  are as before.
